			(description "TVS 12V standoff 600W unidirectional DO-214AA SMB AEC-Q101, VBR 13.3V min, VC 19.9V at 30.2A, IR 1uA max at VRWM, -55 to +150C TJ - 8V8 rail clamp. NOT A ZENER: the D_Zener symbol is only the schematic shape, a zener of the same voltage has orders of magnitude less surge capability and must not be substituted. Cathode (pin 1) to +8V8, anode to GND. THE STANDOFF IS SET BY THE OTP RAIL, NOT THE 8.8V RAIL: fitting R604 lifts the rail to 11.1V for OTP programming, so a 10V part (VBR min 11.1V) would conduct hard the moment R604 goes in. 12V leaves 2.2V to VBR min. Its real job is protecting Q201, not the BQ79616 - LDOIN is regulated by the NPNB loop so it stays at 6V whatever the rail does, but without the clamp Q201 would dissipate (67-6)V x 25mA = 1.5W in SOT-223 and cook; with it, 0.2W. In a mis-regulation fault it sits at about 1.4W, which an SMB cannot hold indefinitely - it will eventually fail short, collapsing the rail and killing the board safely")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "digikey_pn_alt")
				)
				(field
					(name "MPN_alt")
				)
				(field
					(name "digikey_pn") "118-SMBJ12A-QTR-ND")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "SMBJ12A-Q")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "custom_footprints:Bourns_SMBJ-Q_DO-214AA")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet") "https://www.bourns.com/docs/product-datasheets/smbj-q.pdf")
				(field
					(name "Description") "TVS 12V standoff 600W unidirectional DO-214AA SMB AEC-Q101, VBR 13.3V min, VC 19.9V at 30.2A, IR 1uA max at VRWM, -55 to +150C TJ - 8V8 rail clamp. NOT A ZENER: the D_Zener symbol is only the schematic shape, a zener of the same voltage has orders of magnitude less surge capability and must not be substituted. Cathode (pin 1) to +8V8, anode to GND. THE STANDOFF IS SET BY THE OTP RAIL, NOT THE 8.8V RAIL: fitting R604 lifts the rail to 11.1V for OTP programming, so a 10V part (VBR min 11.1V) would conduct hard the moment R604 goes in. 12V leaves 2.2V to VBR min. Its real job is protecting Q201, not the BQ79616 - LDOIN is regulated by the NPNB loop so it stays at 6V whatever the rail does, but without the clamp Q201 would dissipate (67-6)V x 25mA = 1.5W in SOT-223 and cook; with it, 0.2W. In a mis-regulation fault it sits at about 1.4W, which an SMB cannot hold indefinitely - it will eventually fail short, collapsing the rail and killing the board safely")
			)
